; A %{exe:...} reference to a target of this project. It reaches E941 beside
; %{bin:...} as "gen.exe", and the .exe suffix says it is this project's own
; target rather than a binary some package installs, so resolution is never
; asked about it -- and over a whole-project index a name resolution does
; answer nothing for is an answer, not an undecided question. Here to hold
; both: were the gate to treat every scan as partial, this run would report a
; question it can decide. The same reference under a narrowed scan is
; pkg-a/gen/dune.
(executable
 (name gen))

(rule
 (alias check)
 (deps %{exe:gen.exe})
 (action
  (progn)))
